    "_dashboards_comment": "Estate dashboards (`dashboard` tag, apps VLAN). All three render their service list from the SAME published ingress table (modules/proxmox-stack/locals-ingress-backends.tf), so a service is filed on every board by adding its Traefik route \u2014 never by editing three boards. Grouping comes from each backend container's `vlan`, so no second tag list is maintained. Every board is Authelia-gated at the ingress: Glance in particular ships no authentication of its own, so that gate is the only thing in front of it. Homarr is the community-scripts install-layer pilot; Homepage and Glance are file-configured, so their rendered config is idempotent, whereas Homarr's API create always inserts and its role must diff by name.",
    "homarr": {
      "vm_id": 605030,
      "dhcp": true,
      "vlan": "apps",
      "hostname": "homarr",
      "description": "Homarr dashboard \u2014 web UI on 7575 fronted by Traefik; SQLite on its own rootfs. Installed by a borrowed community-scripts installer, which is why its egress includes HTTPS/HTTP.",
      "cpu_cores": 2,
      "memory_dedicated": 1024,
      "tags": [
        "terraform",
        "container",
        "homarr",
        "dashboard"
      ],
      "pool_id": "infrastructure",
      "node_name": "proxmox-1",
      "unprivileged": true,
      "root_disk": {
        "size": 8
      }
    },
    "homepage": {
      "vm_id": 605040,
      "dhcp": true,
      "vlan": "apps",
      "hostname": "homepage",
      "description": "Homepage (gethomepage) service-launcher dashboard \u2014 web UI on 3000 fronted by Traefik; YAML config rendered by Ansible onto rootfs (no mount point, so vzdump captures it without the mount_point backup=1 trap); a byte-identical render is a no-op.",
      "cpu_cores": 1,
      "memory_dedicated": 512,
      "tags": [
        "terraform",
