    "_ai_runner_profiles_comment": "Additional headless AI-runner egress profiles (siblings of the `ai-github` runner). Each is a tag that selects one firewall profile in modules/firewall: `ai-terrakube` (ai_terrakube_rules.tf) = internal-only egress for a runner that drives OpenTofu against the private Terrakube backend \u2014 DNS/NTP/OpenBao + Terrakube API/registry + RustFS S3, and NO WAN at all. `ai-full-net` (ai_full_net_rules.tf) = a coding-agent guest needing general web access \u2014 internal DNS/NTP/OpenBao only + outbound HTTPS (443) to any, still no blanket internal reach. The `ai-runner` tag is the ansible-proxmox-ai inventory group. VMIDs below are illustrative (6-digit positional convention, docs vmid-network-tiers) \u2014 reconcile vm_id against your live deployment.json before applying.",
