    "_ai_runner_comment": "Headless AI execution plane (AI/ML tier 5, ai VLAN). An ai-runner is a confined guest that runs a coding agent (Claude Code / Codex) in permission-skipping mode; the LXC boundary is the ONLY safety control, so the firewall profile is load-bearing. The `ai-github` tag selects the tightest egress profile (modules/firewall/ai_runner_rules.tf): outbound to internal DNS/NTP/OpenBao only + outbound HTTPS to any (github.com + Anthropic/OpenAI are CDN-fronted, no stable dest CIDR). The `ai-runner` tag is the inventory group the ansible-proxmox-ai `ai_runner` role converges. Native installs (Node + npm CLIs) \u2014 plain LXC, no Docker/nesting. VMID follows the 6-digit positional convention (docs vmid-network-tiers); the value here is illustrative. This example omits node_name and uses the default node (same as the sibling AI guests) \u2014 the live guest pins its node in the private deployment.json (the runner host is an idle-capacity node). Reconcile vm_id against your live deployment.json before applying. Other profiles (ai-terrakube, ai-full-net) are follow-ups: each is a new tag + rules file.",
    "ai-runner-01": {
      "vm_id": 515010,
      "node_name": "proxmox-1",
      "dhcp": true,
      "vlan": "ai",
      "hostname": "ai-runner-01",
      "description": "Headless AI job runner \u2014 Claude Code + Codex CLIs in permission-skipping mode, confined by the ai-github firewall egress profile. Polls the Vikunja AI Jobs queue; converged by the ansible-proxmox-ai ai_runner role.",
      "cpu_cores": 4,
      "memory_dedicated": 8192,
      "tags": [
        "terraform",
        "container",
        "ai",
        "ai-runner",
        "ai-github"
      ],
      "pool_id": "ai",
      "unprivileged": true,
      "root_disk": {
        "size": 24
      }
    },
    "_ai_agent_pool_comment": "AI agent POOL (`ai-proxied` profile, modules/firewall/ai_proxied_rules.tf). N identical long-lived guests that pull work from a queue, instead of one guest provisioned per run \u2014 provisioning is amortized and no IaC change is needed to run a task. The profile is strictly tighter than ai-full-net: internal DNS/NTP/OpenBao + the Squid forward proxy + the Cribl AI log-ingest frontends, and NO 443-to-any of its own. Every outbound web request therefore transits the squid guest below, which is where the DOMAIN allowlist is enforced (the Proxmox firewall filters IP/port only, never hostname/SNI). Per-CLI variants (claude / codex / agy) are Squid ACL groups keyed off the client address, NOT separate tags \u2014 at L3/L4 they would be identical rule sets. Grow the pool by copying an entry with the next vm_id; guests are interchangeable, so pool size is a capacity knob with no rule change. Every `ai-runner`-tagged guest must carry exactly one profile tag or the plan fails (variables-containers.tf validation) \u2014 a typo would otherwise leave an agent guest with no firewall at all. VMIDs are illustrative (6-digit positional convention, docs vmid-network-tiers); reconcile against your live deployment.json before applying.",
    "ai-runner-pool-01": {
      "vm_id": 515040,
      "node_name": "proxmox-1",
      "dhcp": true,
      "vlan": "ai",
      "hostname": "ai-runner-pool-01",
      "description": "Pooled AI agent \u2014 pulls jobs from the queue, confined by the ai-proxied firewall profile (no direct WAN; egress only via the Squid allowlist). Converged by the ansible-proxmox-ai ai_runner role.",
      "cpu_cores": 4,
      "memory_dedicated": 8192,
      "tags": [
        "terraform",
        "container",
        "ai",
        "ai-runner",
        "ai-proxied"
      ],
      "pool_id": "ai",
      "unprivileged": true,
      "root_disk": {
        "size": 24
      }
    },
    "ai-runner-pool-02": {
      "vm_id": 515041,
      "node_name": "proxmox-4",
      "dhcp": true,
      "vlan": "ai",
      "hostname": "ai-runner-pool-02",
      "description": "Pooled AI agent \u2014 identical to ai-runner-pool-01; pool members are interchangeable, so scaling out is a copied entry with the next vm_id.",
      "cpu_cores": 4,
      "memory_dedicated": 8192,
      "tags": [
        "terraform",
        "container",
        "ai",
        "ai-runner",
        "ai-proxied"
